  <h2 id="short-answer">The short answer on science careers that involve travel</h2>

  <p>
    Search "science careers that involve travel" and you will find lists that treat it as one glamorous
    destination job. It is not. It is a real, useful filter you can apply to several already-established
    science fields, geology, environmental science, marine biology, wildlife biology, and science
    journalism, each of which already has its own degree path, employer base, and honest pay ceiling on
    this site.
  </p>

  <p>
    The useful question is not "which career lets me travel." It is "which of these underlying sciences do
    I actually want to spend a career studying, and how much of the travel inside it is realistic for my
    life stage, budget, and family situation."
  </p>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      This is a genuinely narrower, thinner topic than most of our career-options guides, and it deserves
      to be treated that way. There is no single "travel scientist" job in India. If a page promises one, it
      is selling a fantasy, not a career map. What follows is the honest cross-section: real fields, real
      institutions, real pay, and a straight answer on how much you will actually travel in each.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="what-travel-means">What "travel" actually means in these careers</h2>

  <p>
    Before comparing tracks, set expectations correctly. In almost every one of these six fields, "travel"
    means one of a few concrete things, not a rotating global itinerary.
  </p>

  <div class="comparison-grid">
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--teal">
      <div class="compare-card__label">What the travel usually looks like</div>
      <ul>
        <li>A field season of a few weeks to a few months at a remote site, camp, or field station, mostly within India.</li>
        <li>Repeated short trips to a project site for sampling, surveying, or assessment, then weeks back at a desk.</li>
        <li>An occasional research cruise, expedition, or assignment, genuinely exciting, but infrequent, not year-round.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--gold">
      <div class="compare-card__label">What it usually does not look like</div>
      <ul>
        <li>Constant international travel or a different country every few months.</li>
        <li>A guaranteed expedition posting straight out of a bachelor's degree.</li>
        <li>Travel as the main job description, with the underlying science treated as secondary.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="track-map">The real tracks, ranked by travel and ceiling</h2>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Track</th>
          <th>What the travel actually looks like</th>
          <th>Typical entry route</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
