            <td data-label="Track"><strong>{item.track}</strong></td>
            <td data-label="What the travel actually looks like">{item.travel}</td>
            <td data-label="Typical entry route">{item.entry}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    Ranked by real, researched growth headroom rather than novelty, geology/mining exploration and
    environmental/EIA fieldwork lead on pay ceiling and offer a genuine independent-consulting ownership
    path. Marine biology runs on a stable but slow government research ladder. Wildlife conservation has
    the most sustained fieldwork and typically the lowest, most unstable pay. Science journalism's ceiling
    depends almost entirely on whether you build a specific niche and audience, not on the entry-level job
    itself. Polar and test-range science are real but rare edge cases, not standalone entry-level careers.
  </p>

  <div class="feature-grid">
    {scalabilityCards.map((item) => (
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-card__label">{item.tier}</div>
        <div class="feature-card__title">{item.title}</div>
