  <h2 id="ai-effect">What AI and remote sensing are changing</h2>

  <p>
    Satellite imagery, drone surveys, and AI-assisted pattern detection are genuinely reducing how many
    routine site visits some of these roles need, satellite-based mineral and land-cover mapping supports
    early-stage geological exploration, remote sensing supports habitat and deforestation monitoring in
    conservation work, and automated ESG and EIA reporting tools are absorbing some of the routine
    data-crunching in environmental consulting. None of this removes the fieldwork; it moves where the value
    sits. The geologist, ecologist, or environmental scientist who can verify and defend what a satellite or
    sensor flagged, and who can still run the on-ground work a remote tool cannot replace, keeps growing
    their pay. The one who can only produce a routine report does not.
  </p>

