  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take on the scalable-ownership path</p>
    <p>
      Most of the fixed, fieldwork-heavy roles here, GSI and ONGC geology, NIO/CMFRI marine research, WII
      and NGO wildlife work, run on government or fellowship-linked pay scales with a real but slow and
      capped ceiling. The genuine <strong>scalable-ownership paths</strong> in this space are narrower and
      specific: senior expedition or project leadership inside a large exploration or research programme,
      independent environmental or geological consulting built on years of client relationships, and, for
      strong communicators, a science-journalism or content specialty built deliberately around one
      fieldwork niche. None of these are fast, and none are guaranteed, but they are the real ceiling-raising
      moves in this space, not the entry-level fieldwork itself.
    </p>
  </div>

